  "scope": [
    "One continuous deterministic local encounter in the actual Battle scene on authored Harbor terrain; campaign persistence disabled for this visual review.",
    "Shared fixture begins from the same populated Harbor world as Battle, preserves monotonically assigned unit IDs, and replaces only the initial forces and strategic clocks.",
    "Ordinary command APIs and full 30 Hz simulation ticks produce concurrent digging, automatic frag preparation and a real covering shot in one section.",
    "Accepted replacements cancel an unspent smoke preparation, preserve already released frag and smoke payloads, and resume the same physical work site.",
    "Visible native smoke agrees with forward and reverse optical query obstruction, and the lane becomes clear when its finite world effect expires.",
    "The delegated reserve physically approaches, fires, delivers a sustained useful interval, returns to its original assignment and releases its temporary ownership.",
    "The same site progresses through survey, hasty cover and reinforcement; duplicate orders and paid pause/resume charge only 50 supply.",
    "All eight captures are inspected at the minimum 1280 x 800 physical window, including requested UI scale 1.5 for active reinforcement, interruption and completion. Command bounds, roster clearance and actual bold-font label fit are checked.",
    "Per-capture member inventory and support state are copied before the next phase, preserving the historical state of each screenshot. Actual Battle input, atlas, save/reload and retry inventory transitions are covered separately by test_m1_campaign_flow.gd."
  ],
  "visual_findings": [
    "The defender, engineer, reserve, opposing section and work site remain in the same Harbor clearing across all eight captures; reserve movement, casualty remains and progressing work are visible.",
    "The selected section shows Digging with 17 seconds remaining during concurrent roles, then Preparing smoke grenade after its work order is replaced. The frag label drops from 3 to 2 only after release.",
    "The cloud renders seven puffs over its actual optical volume while work resumes; the same frontage tests blocked in both directions. The hasty site completes while the smoke is still visible.",
    "At requested UI scale 1.5, the engineer shows Reinforcing with 8 seconds remaining. During Hold, its actor claim is released and the visible hasty structure remains while paid progress stays unchanged for 0.6 simulated seconds.",
    "Final capture shows the reinforced structure, returned reserve, clear expired smoke lane and 950 remaining supply. Compact commands and group roster remain within the viewport without overlapping."
  ],
